{"id": "EUVD-2026-76265", "enisaUuid": "aef54945-84cd-36cb-831c-dc0e9e0552b0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: rtlwifi: rtl8192du: Fix possible memory leak in rtl92du_init_sw_vars()\n\nThe memory allocated inside rtl92du_init_shared_data() is not freed in\nany of the subsequent error paths in rtl92du_init_sw_vars().\nFix that by adding a call to rtl92du_deinit_shared_data() in the error\npath.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:26", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a5b23e7dbeb00c93ec3b8add97f5de9bb9cbb5c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc8b0be0ec4d9b0c80f07b27e656e4a94de5a344", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7159e1e12468a0b1ac519b296280c0a27f91eab5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6496ce90845df2d22fb8e8ed235cd2936fad41c8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-26cr-hp89-hvf4", "CVE-2026-80942"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c7c3999-6091-3225-878a-d36b739af3aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "32b433ec-b836-3a4e-8584-45d41b86536e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b5dc8873b6ffebd331e46814e537179eac8b6aa4 <6496ce90845df2d22fb8e8ed235cd2936fad41c8"}, {"id": "486ef4b1-b495-324d-ab78-a5896635ce40", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b5dc8873b6ffebd331e46814e537179eac8b6aa4 <dc8b0be0ec4d9b0c80f07b27e656e4a94de5a344"}, {"id": "5443f87f-067c-31ba-96bd-eac35f4c365a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "58f07ec0-6f3a-3ba8-937b-d06f4f32c0fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "85d2e7b9-56da-323f-a779-97c0e2b1225c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b5dc8873b6ffebd331e46814e537179eac8b6aa4 <3a5b23e7dbeb